gpui: Tell the running app that this host moves the keyboard natively

Against longbridge/nsh e626a8d (0.4.0), after patches 0001-0003 and 0006.
An app that works around the prebuilt host's web view focus defects
(typing forwarded through the keymap while a WKWebView stays first
responder, pages blurred by script to hand the keyboard back) must not do
so on a host that has patches 0001 and 0002: there the keyboard really
moves, and the workarounds type every key twice or blur a page the user
just clicked into. The app cannot find this out by trying (`focus()` on a
web view takes the keyboard, `blur()` blurs every field on the prebuilt
host), so the host says it: `host.call("webview.nativeFocus")` resolves
`true`. A host without this handler rejects the call. Only apply this
together with 0001 and 0002.

## Public API

- `webview.nativeFocus()`: a `host.call` name of the development host
  (declare it in `nsh.json`'s `capabilities.host`). Resolves `true`.

